Coordination Rules	Interaction semantics
Completion Criteria	Overall success conditions
Governance Domain	Responsible authority
8. Workflow Dependencies

Atlas defines canonical dependency types.

Dependency	Description
Sequential	One workflow starts after another completes
Parallel	Concurrent execution
Conditional	Depends on evaluation outcome
Event-Driven	Triggered by Canonical Events
Data Dependency	Requires outputs from another workflow
Resource Dependency	Requires shared resources

Dependencies SHALL be explicitly declared.

9. Synchronization

Atlas supports the following synchronization patterns.

Pattern	Description
Barrier	Wait for all workflows
Join	Merge execution paths
Wait-for-All	Continue after all complete
Wait-for-Any	Continue after first completion
Majority	Continue after quorum
Time Window	Synchronize within defined period

Synchronization SHALL preserve deterministic execution.

10. Event-Driven Coordination

Workflow orchestration MAY respond to:

Workflow Started
Workflow Completed
Activity Completed
Activity Failed
Policy Decision
External Event
Digital Twin Update
AI Recommendation

Events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

11. Distributed Execution

Atlas supports execution across:

Organizations
Geographic regions
Cloud environments
Edge environments
Digital Twins
AI agents
External systems

Distributed execution SHALL preserve workflow semantics.

12. Compensation Workflows

When recovery requires reversing completed work, orchestration MAY invoke Compensation Workflows.

Compensation SHALL define:

Target workflow
Trigger condition
Recovery objective
Compensating activities
Completion criteria

Compensation SHALL preserve execution history.

